      "output": "# Port simulation core: reproducible, pure JavaScript\n\nNothing in this code runs on its own. A caller makes the first state with `s=init(seed)` and then calls `s=step(s)` every 2 seconds. The caller owns the timer, pause and speed control. `step` deep-copies its input, so it never changes the previous state.\n\n```js\nfunction rnd(s){let t=s.r=s.r+0x6D2B79F5|0;t=Math.imul(t^t>>>15,t|1);t^=t+Math.imul(t^t>>>7,t|61);return((t^t>>>14)>>>0)/4294967296}\nvar CAP=100,TM=6,DAY=240;\nfunction init(seed){var s={r:seed|0,tick:0,nid:1,ships:[],cranes:[],yards:[],day:{moves:0,ships:0},events:[]};\nfor(let i=0;i<4;i++)s.cranes.push({id:i,berth:-1,working:false,rate:25+(rnd(s)*11|0),acc:0,moves:0});\nfor(let i=0;i<6;i++)s.yards.push(30+(rnd(s)*30|0));met(s,0);return s}\nfunction step(p){var s=JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(p)),e=s.events=[],u=[],Y=s.yards,mv=0;\nif(++s.tick%DAY==0){s.day={moves:0,ships:0};e.push('New day')}\ns.ships=s.ships.filter(x=>!(x.phase=='departing'&&--x.t<=0&&(s.day.ships++,e.push(x.id+' left berth '+x.berth))));\nfor(const x of s.ships){if(x.phase=='berthing'&&--x.t<=0){x.phase='working';e.push(x.id+' working at berth '+x.berth)}if(x.berth>=0)u[x.berth]=1}\nfor(const x of s.ships)if(x.phase=='waiting')for(let b=0;b<3;b++)if(!u[b]){u[b]=1;Object.assign(x,{phase:'berthing',berth:b,t:1});e.push(x.id+' berthing at '+b);break}\nif(rnd(s)<.3&&s.ships.filter(x=>x.phase=='waiting').length<5){const id='S'+s.nid++;s.ships.push({id,phase:'waiting',berth:-1,load:60+(rnd(s)*140|0),t:0});e.push(id+' arrived at anchorage')}\nconst w=s.ships.filter(x=>x.phase=='working').sort((a,b)=>a.berth-b.berth);\nfor(const c of s.cranes){const h=w[c.id%w.length];c.berth=h?h.berth:-1;c.working=false;if(!h){c.acc=0;continue}\nc.acc+=c.rate*TM/60;let n=c.acc|0;c.acc-=n;\nwhile(n-->0&&h.load>0){const d=h.load%2;let k=0;for(let j=1;j<6;j++)if(d?Y[j]<Y[k]:Y[j]>Y[k])k=j;\nif(d?Y[k]>=CAP:Y[k]<=0){e.push('Crane '+c.id+' blocked: yard '+(d?'full':'empty'));c.acc=0;break}\nY[k]+=d?1:-1;h.load--;c.moves++;s.day.moves++;mv++;c.working=true}}\nfor(const x of w)if(x.load<=0){x.phase='departing';x.t=1;e.push(x.id+' done, departing')}\nfor(let k=0;k<6;k++)Y[k]=Math.max(0,Math.min(CAP,Y[k]+(rnd(s)*5|0)-2));\nmet(s,mv);return s}\nfunction met(s,mv){const m=s.tick%DAY*TM,q=f=>s.ships.filter(f).length,z=n=>('0'+n).slice(-2);\ns.metrics={clock:z(m/60|0)+':'+z(m%60),berthOcc:Math.round(q(x=>x.berth>=0)/3*100),cranesWorking:s.cranes.filter(c=>c.working).length,craneMovesTick:mv,craneMovesTotal:s.cranes.reduce((a,c)=>a+c.moves,0),yardOcc:Math.round(Y0(s)/6/CAP*100),blockOcc:s.yards.map(v=>Math.round(v/CAP*100)),shipsWaiting:q(x=>x.phase=='waiting'),shipsDoneToday:s.day.ships,throughputToday:s.day.moves}}\nfunction Y0(s){return s.yards.reduce((a,v)=>a+v,0)}\n```\n\n## State\n- **ships**: each ship has `id`, `phase`, `berth`, `load` and a phase timer `t`.\n  - `phase` is one of `waiting`, `berthing`, `working` or `departing`.\n  - `berth` is 0–2, or −1 while the ship waits at anchorage.\n  - `load` is the number of container moves still to do.\n- **cranes**: there are 4 cranes, ids 0–3.\n  - Each crane has `berth` (−1 when idle) and `working`.\n  - Each crane has a `rate` in moves per hour, `acc` (fractional moves carried over) and `moves` (its cumulative total).\n- **yards**: 6 numbers, one per block 0–5, each holding 0 to `CAP` (100) boxes.\n- **metrics**: the derived values listed below.\n- **events**: the texts describing what happened in this tick.\n- **r**: the seed state of mulberry32, carried inside `state` so that runs can be reproduced.\n\n## Rules\n- **Time:** each tick is 2 s of real time and 6 simulated minutes. A simulated day is 240 ticks; at the end of it, the daily counters reset to 0.\n- **Ship arrivals:** a new ship arrives with probability 0.3 per tick, unless 5 ships are already waiting. Its `load` is 60–199 moves.\n- **Ship phases:**\n  1. `waiting` → `berthing`: happens when a berth is free, oldest waiting ship first. Berthing lasts 1 tick.\n  2. `berthing` → `working`: happens after that tick.\n  3. `working` → `departing`: happens when `load` reaches 0. Departing lasts 1 tick, and then the ship and its berth are freed.\n- **Crane assignment:** the cranes are spread over the working ships, sorted by berth, using `id % count`.\n- **Crane rates:** each crane works at 25–35 moves per hour, fixed by the seed. That gives `rate×6/60`, about 2.5–3.5 moves per tick, with fractions carried over to the next tick.\n- **Yard rules:**\n  - A move on an odd remaining `load` is a discharge: it adds 1 box to the emptiest block.\n  - A move on an even remaining `load` is a load: it takes 1 box from the fullest block.\n  - If the target block is full (discharge) or empty (load), the crane is blocked and records an event.\n  - Gate trucks then change each block by −2 to +2 boxes.\n  - Every value is clamped to 0–`CAP`, so yard occupancy never goes past 100%.\n\n## Metrics\n| Metric | What it means |\n|---|---|\n| `berthOcc` | Berths holding a ship (berthing, working or departing) ÷ 3 × 100. The maximum is 100%. |\n| `cranesWorking`, `craneMovesTick` | Cranes that made at least one move this tick, and the number of moves made this tick. |\n| `craneMovesTotal` | Sum of all crane moves since `init`. |\n| `yardOcc`, `blockOcc` | Average fill of all 6 blocks in %, and the fill of each block in % (each 0–100). |\n| `shipsWaiting` | Ships at anchorage. |\n| `throughputToday`, `shipsDoneToday` | Container moves handled today, and ships that have departed today. |\n| `clock` | Simulated time of day, as HH:MM. |\n\n## Not yet verified (the code has not been run in this node)\n- Whether it runs without errors, and its exact length. I counted it by hand at about 2,400–2,500 characters.\n- That two runs with the same seed give identical states, and that occupancy stays at or below 100% over a long run. The logic is written to guarantee both, but neither has been tested.\n- Whether yard occupancy drifts over a long run. Truck flow is symmetric on average, so this has not been tuned."
